// duplicate) all die at `bech32_verify_checksum`, so a few hundred of them pin
// that behaviour down.  The interesting boundaries are the ones a tamper can
// reach *before* the checksum (separator position, ord 33..126, mixed case,
// hrp <= 83, pos + 7 > len) and the ones it reaches *after*, if the tampered
// payload is re-checksummed (witness version, program length, pad=false
